Version 0.2.0
-------------
The hermetic rust_repo release: third-party crates as generated subrepos,
with cargo's contract reimplemented offline (no cargo anywhere but the
bootstrap egg).

  * rust_repo: crates.io subrepos with generated BUILD files; git-forge
    sources for forks (download= / git_repo=); runnable bin crates.
  * please_rust: generate / compile / build-script / resolve / sync /
    lock / test subcommands; self-hosted via these rules; 82 unit tests.
  * Resolution in the build graph (rust_resolve): semver version routing
    and cargo resolver-v2 feature unification, with host/target build
    units split like cargo's.
  * sync maintains the third-party BUILD (explicit direct/indirect
    declarations, pruning, sha256 hashes, Cargo.lock import); lock adds
    dependencies from the crates.io sparse index without cargo.
  * First-party rules on the same driver: rust_library (all crate
    types), rust_binary (statically linked by default), rust_test with
    per-test results, integration tests, rust_doc_test, rust_benchmark.
  * proto/gRPC: vendored language definition, protoc-gen-prost/tonic
    built from their crates.
  * Toolchain: Rust 1.97.1, sha256-pinned; C compiler via the cc
    plugin's configuration; CONFIG knobs for all tools.
  * e2e consumer-repo test and CI workflow.

Version 0.1.0
-------------
  * Initial rust_crate-based rules.
